1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,282
Why did Ford build a Mustang to

2
00:00:02,282 --> 00:00:03,239
beat Porsche?

3
00:00:03,419 --> 00:00:04,954
Here is the honest answer,

4
00:00:04,954 --> 00:00:06,844
and it starts with a correction.

5
00:00:07,024 --> 00:00:09,268
None of the sources we read says

6
00:00:09,268 --> 00:00:11,652
Ford built the Mustang GTD to beat

7
00:00:11,652 --> 00:00:12,213
Porsche.

8
00:00:12,393 --> 00:00:14,819
What they do say is stranger and

9
00:00:14,819 --> 00:00:17,396
more specific: a Le Mans race car,

10
00:00:17,396 --> 00:00:19,745
a chief executive who liked it,

11
00:00:19,745 --> 00:00:22,626
a seven-minute lap of the Nürburgring,

12
00:00:22,626 --> 00:00:25,733
and a Canadian company called Multimatic.

13
00:00:25,913 --> 00:00:27,089
This is the story,

14
00:00:27,089 --> 00:00:28,723
with every claim sourced.

15
00:00:29,073 --> 00:00:30,894
We read Torque Café,

16
00:00:30,894 --> 00:00:32,990
Design News, Motor One,

17
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:36,178
The Drive, AutoGuide and Wikipedia.

18
00:00:36,358 --> 00:00:38,856
We will tell you what Ford's executives

19
00:00:38,856 --> 00:00:40,393
said in their own words,

20
00:00:40,393 --> 00:00:41,930
what the lap times were,

21
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:43,916
and where the sources disagree.

22
00:00:44,096 --> 00:00:46,276
We will also tell you what nobody

23
00:00:46,276 --> 00:00:46,871
has said.

24
00:00:47,051 --> 00:00:49,160
And we will show you why Porsche

25
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:50,544
belongs in the story,

26
00:00:50,544 --> 00:00:52,850
even though no source puts it there

27
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:53,773
as the target.

28
00:00:54,123 --> 00:00:56,669
The story begins with a race car,

29
00:00:56,669 --> 00:00:57,826
not a road car.

30
00:00:58,006 --> 00:01:00,383
Wikipedia says the Mustang GT3,

31
00:01:00,383 --> 00:01:04,064
developed by Ford Performance and Multimatic and

32
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,904
based on the Dark Horse,

33
00:01:05,904 --> 00:01:08,664
was revealed in twenty twenty-three.

34
00:01:08,844 --> 00:01:12,630
It races in the IMSA SportsCar Championship

35
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:16,240
and the FIA World Endurance Championship.

36
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:19,556
Torque Café says the Mustang Dark Horse

37
00:01:19,556 --> 00:01:22,532
is the homologation model for the GT3

38
00:01:22,532 --> 00:01:23,014
entry.

39
00:01:23,364 --> 00:01:25,600
The race car took the Mustang back

40
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,324
to Le Mans.

41
00:01:26,504 --> 00:01:29,007
Wikipedia says it raced there for the

42
00:01:29,007 --> 00:01:31,646
first time since nineteen ninety-seven,

43
00:01:31,646 --> 00:01:33,540
a gap of twenty-seven years.

44
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:37,120
Proton Competition became the first customer team

45
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,618
in the World Endurance Championship.

46
00:01:39,798 --> 00:01:42,210
Design News says Larry Holt,

47
00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:45,483
Multimatic's chief technology officer,

48
00:01:45,483 --> 00:01:47,981
supervised the GT3 programme,

49
00:01:47,981 --> 00:01:51,168
which finished third in the GT3 class

50
00:01:51,168 --> 00:01:52,116
at Le Mans.

51
00:01:52,466 --> 00:01:55,499
Torque Café quotes Ford's chief executive,

52
00:01:55,499 --> 00:01:57,810
Jim Farley, at the launch of the

53
00:01:57,810 --> 00:02:01,998
seventh-generation Mustang in September twenty twenty-two:

54
00:02:01,998 --> 00:02:03,804
to go to Le Mans you need

55
00:02:03,804 --> 00:02:04,598
a road car.

56
00:02:04,778 --> 00:02:06,668
That is a single sentence,

57
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,850
but it is the closest thing in

58
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:10,595
our sources to a reason.

59
00:02:10,775 --> 00:02:14,560
The racing programme needed a road-going version,

60
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,800
and the road car was the GTD.

61
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,559
That is Farley's logic as quoted,

62
00:02:19,559 --> 00:02:21,357
not our interpretation.

63
00:02:21,707 --> 00:02:24,960
Torque Café also quotes Mark Rushbrook,

64
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:27,128
who runs Ford Performance.

65
00:02:27,308 --> 00:02:29,215
He says: we don't want to make

66
00:02:29,215 --> 00:02:31,694
boring cars, and to have something like

67
00:02:31,694 --> 00:02:33,601
this, it is a passion product.

68
00:02:33,781 --> 00:02:35,890
And he says that as soon as

69
00:02:35,890 --> 00:02:38,077
Jim saw the GT3 there was no

70
00:02:38,077 --> 00:02:38,936
hesitation.

71
00:02:39,116 --> 00:02:41,018
So by Rushbrook's account,

72
00:02:41,018 --> 00:02:42,628
the decision was fast,

73
00:02:42,628 --> 00:02:45,116
and it was driven by enthusiasm as

74
00:02:45,116 --> 00:02:47,092
much as by any spreadsheet.

75
00:02:47,442 --> 00:02:49,687
Executive chairman Bill Ford,

76
00:02:49,687 --> 00:02:51,777
quoted in the same article,

77
00:02:51,777 --> 00:02:54,487
says: we want to take everything to

78
00:02:54,487 --> 00:02:56,965
the apex and just do whatever is

79
00:02:56,965 --> 00:02:59,133
possible with that platform.

80
00:02:59,313 --> 00:03:01,318
He adds that the GTD is an

81
00:03:01,318 --> 00:03:02,784
expression of that.

82
00:03:02,964 --> 00:03:05,620
Notice what is missing from all three

83
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:06,122
quotes.

84
00:03:06,302 --> 00:03:08,440
There is no rival named,

85
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,488
no Porsche, no Ferrari,

86
00:03:10,488 --> 00:03:12,270
and no sales target.

87
00:03:12,450 --> 00:03:14,598
The stated motives are Le Mans,

88
00:03:14,598 --> 00:03:16,954
passion and the platform's limits.

89
00:03:17,305 --> 00:03:20,341
Torque Café says Farley first hinted at

90
00:03:20,341 --> 00:03:23,377
the GTD in September twenty twenty-two.

91
00:03:23,557 --> 00:03:26,630
Its article is dated the twenty-sixth of

92
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:28,551
June, twenty twenty-four,

93
00:03:28,551 --> 00:03:31,778
and quotes Rushbrook speaking at the GTD's

94
00:03:31,778 --> 00:03:35,005
public display at the twenty-four Hours of

95
00:03:35,005 --> 00:03:35,619
Le Mans.

96
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:37,095
By our arithmetic,

97
00:03:37,095 --> 00:03:40,046
that is about twenty-one months from hint

98
00:03:40,046 --> 00:03:40,838
to article.

99
00:03:41,018 --> 00:03:43,202
Ford was using the race as its

100
00:03:43,202 --> 00:03:45,604
stage, which fits Farley's logic.

101
00:03:45,954 --> 00:03:48,322
Behind the badge is Multimatic.

102
00:03:48,502 --> 00:03:51,563
Torque Café describes it as a Canadian

103
00:03:51,563 --> 00:03:54,704
company that builds the Mustang GT3 and

104
00:03:54,704 --> 00:03:58,006
supplies the chassis for the Porsche nine

105
00:03:58,006 --> 00:04:00,100
sixty-three LMDh race car.

106
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,442
It will also assemble the GTD,

107
00:04:02,442 --> 00:04:05,180
rather than Ford building it directly.

108
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:08,360
This is the first place Porsche appears,

109
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,935
and it is a surprise:

110
00:04:09,935 --> 00:04:13,311
the Mustang's builder also supplies a Porsche

111
00:04:13,311 --> 00:04:13,986
race car.

112
00:04:14,336 --> 00:04:16,431
That does not mean Porsche helped build

113
00:04:16,431 --> 00:04:17,075
the Mustang.

114
00:04:17,255 --> 00:04:19,357
Nothing in our sources says so.

115
00:04:19,537 --> 00:04:22,216
It means the company that makes the

116
00:04:22,216 --> 00:04:24,972
Mustang GTD also works for a Porsche

117
00:04:24,972 --> 00:04:28,569
racing programme, which is a normal arrangement

118
00:04:28,569 --> 00:04:29,794
in motor racing,

119
00:04:29,794 --> 00:04:33,086
where specialist firms serve several teams.

120
00:04:33,266 --> 00:04:35,272
We mention it because it shows how

121
00:04:35,272 --> 00:04:36,865
connected these rivals are.

122
00:04:37,045 --> 00:04:39,754
The sources stop at the fact; the

123
00:04:39,754 --> 00:04:41,642
interpretation is ours.

124
00:04:41,993 --> 00:04:45,535
Design News adds that Multimatic built the

125
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:48,909
GT3 and GTD and supplied the spool-valve

126
00:04:48,909 --> 00:04:50,259
shock absorbers.

127
00:04:50,439 --> 00:04:53,248
Larry Holt says the GTD has inboard

128
00:04:53,248 --> 00:04:56,137
suspension like prototype race cars,

129
00:04:56,137 --> 00:04:59,267
a dual-element rear wing with an active

130
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:01,433
flap, and two ride heights.

131
00:05:01,613 --> 00:05:04,557
Torque Café says Ford claims the transaxle

132
00:05:04,557 --> 00:05:08,202
and carbon driveshaft give almost fifty-fifty weight

133
00:05:08,202 --> 00:05:09,114
distribution.

134
00:05:09,464 --> 00:05:11,484
The Drive puts it more bluntly:

135
00:05:11,484 --> 00:05:14,546
Multimatic massaged the chassis and suspension,

136
00:05:14,546 --> 00:05:16,827
and the car shares very little with

137
00:05:16,827 --> 00:05:18,717
a regular Mustang underneath.

138
00:05:18,897 --> 00:05:20,754
That is the outlet's description.

139
00:05:20,934 --> 00:05:22,647
It means the GTD is not a

140
00:05:22,647 --> 00:05:25,456
hot-rodded Mustang, it is a different car

141
00:05:25,456 --> 00:05:27,169
wearing the Mustang name.

142
00:05:27,349 --> 00:05:29,226
That helps explain the price,

143
00:05:29,226 --> 00:05:31,685
which The Drive gives as three hundred

144
00:05:31,685 --> 00:05:33,885
twenty-five thousand dollars plus.

145
00:05:34,236 --> 00:05:35,582
Now the promise.

146
00:05:35,762 --> 00:05:38,353
AutoGuide reported that at the debut in

147
00:05:38,353 --> 00:05:40,146
August twenty twenty-three,

148
00:05:40,146 --> 00:05:42,936
Farley promised a Nürburgring lap in under

149
00:05:42,936 --> 00:05:43,866
seven minutes.

150
00:05:44,046 --> 00:05:47,161
Design News quotes chief engineer Greg Goodall

151
00:05:47,161 --> 00:05:49,733
tying the engineering to the quest for

152
00:05:49,733 --> 00:05:51,291
a sub-seven-minute lap.

153
00:05:51,471 --> 00:05:54,222
We could only confirm the target from

154
00:05:54,222 --> 00:05:55,561
those two reports,

155
00:05:55,561 --> 00:05:57,717
not read the original speech,

156
00:05:57,717 --> 00:05:59,725
so we attribute it to them.

157
00:06:00,076 --> 00:06:02,429
The Nordschleife is the point of the

158
00:06:02,429 --> 00:06:05,043
whole project, and Ford chose it because

159
00:06:05,043 --> 00:06:07,134
it is the lap everyone compares.

160
00:06:07,314 --> 00:06:10,252
Seven minutes is four hundred twenty seconds.

161
00:06:10,432 --> 00:06:11,764
By our arithmetic,

162
00:06:11,764 --> 00:06:14,577
that is the line every GTD engineering

163
00:06:14,577 --> 00:06:16,354
decision was pointed at,

164
00:06:16,354 --> 00:06:17,909
according to Goodall.

165
00:06:18,089 --> 00:06:20,956
Anything slower would have been a failure

166
00:06:20,956 --> 00:06:22,004
of the promise,

167
00:06:22,004 --> 00:06:24,172
and anything faster a headline.

168
00:06:24,523 --> 00:06:26,380
The power figure moved too.

169
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:29,566
Design News and Torque Café describe an

170
00:06:29,566 --> 00:06:32,726
engine of about eight hundred horsepower,

171
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:35,732
a five point two litre supercharged V8.

172
00:06:35,912 --> 00:06:37,777
Ford's stated final output,

173
00:06:37,777 --> 00:06:40,333
according to Motor One and The Drive,

174
00:06:40,333 --> 00:06:42,059
is eight hundred fifteen,

175
00:06:42,059 --> 00:06:45,444
with six hundred sixty-four pound-feet of torque.

176
00:06:45,624 --> 00:06:48,203
So eight hundred was the earlier report,

177
00:06:48,203 --> 00:06:50,396
fifteen more was the final figure.

178
00:06:50,746 --> 00:06:53,389
Design News makes one more point:

179
00:06:53,389 --> 00:06:55,953
the GTD can make more power than

180
00:06:55,953 --> 00:06:57,315
the GT3 race car,

181
00:06:57,315 --> 00:06:59,959
because it is not bound by racing

182
00:06:59,959 --> 00:07:00,440
rules.

183
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:02,354
That is the key to the whole

184
00:07:02,354 --> 00:07:02,849
project.

185
00:07:03,029 --> 00:07:05,201
The race car must obey a class

186
00:07:05,201 --> 00:07:05,781
formula.

187
00:07:05,961 --> 00:07:07,563
The road car does not.

188
00:07:07,743 --> 00:07:10,217
So Ford could build a road car

189
00:07:10,217 --> 00:07:12,773
faster than its own race car on

190
00:07:12,773 --> 00:07:14,752
power, which is unusual,

191
00:07:14,752 --> 00:07:17,556
and it explains why the GTD exists

192
00:07:17,556 --> 00:07:18,134
at all.

193
00:07:18,484 --> 00:07:19,366
Then the lap.

194
00:07:19,546 --> 00:07:22,333
Motor One reports that Dirk Müller of

195
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:26,251
Multimatic Motorsports lapped the Nürburgring in six

196
00:07:26,251 --> 00:07:29,942
minutes, fifty-seven point six eight five seconds

197
00:07:29,942 --> 00:07:31,826
on the seventh of August,

198
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:33,257
twenty twenty-four.

199
00:07:33,437 --> 00:07:35,362
Ford announced it on the tenth of

200
00:07:35,362 --> 00:07:35,887
December.

201
00:07:36,067 --> 00:07:37,427
By our arithmetic,

202
00:07:37,427 --> 00:07:40,676
that is one hundred twenty-five days later.

203
00:07:40,856 --> 00:07:42,882
The Drive agrees on the time and

204
00:07:42,882 --> 00:07:44,780
calls Müller a Le Mans winner.

205
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:46,619
By our arithmetic,

206
00:07:46,619 --> 00:07:49,843
six fifty-seven point six eight five is

207
00:07:49,843 --> 00:07:53,397
four hundred seventeen point six eight five

208
00:07:53,397 --> 00:07:54,059
seconds.

209
00:07:54,239 --> 00:07:56,249
That is two point three one five

210
00:07:56,249 --> 00:07:58,511
seconds under the seven-minute line.

211
00:07:58,691 --> 00:08:00,362
It is not a large margin,

212
00:08:00,362 --> 00:08:02,633
which is why every tenth mattered,

213
00:08:02,633 --> 00:08:04,972
and why Farley's promise was risky.

214
00:08:05,152 --> 00:08:06,957
Two seconds on a lap of that

215
00:08:06,957 --> 00:08:08,890
length is a very thin cushion.

216
00:08:09,241 --> 00:08:11,842
Motor One says the lap was the

217
00:08:11,842 --> 00:08:15,484
fastest by a North American production car

218
00:08:15,484 --> 00:08:18,172
and beat the Dodge Viper ACR by

219
00:08:18,172 --> 00:08:20,340
four point three seconds.

220
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:23,765
The Drive says the previous American record

221
00:08:23,765 --> 00:08:25,953
was the Viper ACR at seven oh

222
00:08:25,953 --> 00:08:27,387
one point three oh,

223
00:08:27,387 --> 00:08:28,972
held for seven years,

224
00:08:28,972 --> 00:08:31,839
and calls the GTD roughly five seconds

225
00:08:31,839 --> 00:08:32,443
quicker.

226
00:08:32,623 --> 00:08:34,964
Our notes also list a Viper time

227
00:08:34,964 --> 00:08:37,232
of seven oh one point oh three.

228
00:08:37,412 --> 00:08:39,421
These do not agree with each other.

229
00:08:39,771 --> 00:08:41,071
Let us do the sums.

230
00:08:41,251 --> 00:08:44,196
Against seven oh one point three oh,

231
00:08:44,196 --> 00:08:46,650
the GTD is three point six one

232
00:08:46,650 --> 00:08:48,287
five seconds faster.

233
00:08:48,467 --> 00:08:50,958
Against seven oh one point oh three,

234
00:08:50,958 --> 00:08:53,241
it is three point three four five

235
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:53,726
faster.

236
00:08:53,906 --> 00:08:56,855
Neither is four point three or five.

237
00:08:57,035 --> 00:08:59,480
So the three sources give three different

238
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:01,688
margins, and we cannot tell you which

239
00:09:01,688 --> 00:09:02,224
is right.

240
00:09:02,404 --> 00:09:04,785
All agree on the direction:

241
00:09:04,785 --> 00:09:08,048
the GTD was quicker than any American

242
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:10,253
production car before it.

243
00:09:10,603 --> 00:09:12,692
Motor One adds context.

244
00:09:12,872 --> 00:09:14,967
It says the GTD was one of

245
00:09:14,967 --> 00:09:18,350
six production sports cars worldwide to go

246
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:19,961
under seven minutes,

247
00:09:19,961 --> 00:09:22,056
and the only American one.

248
00:09:22,236 --> 00:09:25,520
The Drive says only five production cars

249
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:26,833
had gone faster.

250
00:09:27,013 --> 00:09:29,935
These agree, once you count the GTD

251
00:09:29,935 --> 00:09:30,520
itself.

252
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:34,261
Motor One names the Mercedes-AMG One at

253
00:09:34,261 --> 00:09:37,548
six twenty-nine point oh nine as the

254
00:09:37,548 --> 00:09:39,923
overall production record,

255
00:09:39,923 --> 00:09:42,662
and the AMG GT Black Series at

256
00:09:42,662 --> 00:09:45,949
six forty-three point six one as the

257
00:09:45,949 --> 00:09:48,324
fastest front-engined car.

258
00:09:48,674 --> 00:09:51,272
Farley's quote, in both Motor One and

259
00:09:51,272 --> 00:09:52,256
The Drive, is:

260
00:09:52,256 --> 00:09:54,223
we are proud to be the first

261
00:09:54,223 --> 00:09:56,892
American automaker with a car that can

262
00:09:56,892 --> 00:09:59,912
lap the Nürburgring in under seven minutes.

263
00:10:00,092 --> 00:10:02,429
He adds: we know there is much

264
00:10:02,429 --> 00:10:05,155
